WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.181 --> 00:00:02.764
(gentle music)

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:07.210
- [Zoe] Thousands of people
come into the United States

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:09.400
each day with nothing.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.830
Some of them become
day laborers and end up

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.860
in detention centers when
detained by authorities.

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.850
But outside these federal prisons,

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.850
a band called Los Jornaleros del Norte

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.760
sends a message of hope.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.677
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.792
(singing in foreign language)

00:00:36.792 --> 00:00:39.375
(gentle music)

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.970
- I'm Zoe Saldana from BESE,

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.740
and I'm teaming up with Great
Big Story to shine a light

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.114
on American Latinx excellence
around the country.

00:00:52.114 --> 00:00:54.531
(soft music)

00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:01.656
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:07.441 --> 00:02:11.420
(lively Mexican music)

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:13.690
- [Zoe] The band plays
all over the country,

00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:15.050
but they have a special connection

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:18.920
to one place in particular:
(singing in foreign language)

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:21.670
the detention center in
downtown Los Angeles.

00:02:21.670 --> 00:02:24.260
It primarily houses undocumented workers

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.574
who have been arrested
and face deportation.

00:02:26.574 --> 00:02:30.500
(singing in foreign language)

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.020
In 2010, the band marched in front

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.660
of the gigantic building,
singing songs of protest

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.520
to raise awareness for
the unfair deportation

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.610
of the people waiting inside.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:43.400
The band continues to do
these concerts to this day

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.793
but will never forget
that first experience.

00:02:48.254 --> 00:02:52.171
(speaking in foreign language)

00:03:36.528 --> 00:03:39.049
(gentle music)

00:03:39.049 --> 00:03:42.966
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:09.452 --> 00:04:13.035
(gentle electronic music)

